What is Ferrotitanium?
Ferrotitanium is a strategic ferroalloy combining iron and titanium (typically 35% or 70% Ti content), with trace carbon. First isolated in 1798 and later refined in 1895, this alloy demonstrates unique characteristics including high reactivity with oxygen/nitrogen, low density, exceptional strength-to-weight ratio, and superior corrosion resistance. These properties make it indispensable for manufacturing advanced steels in demanding applications.

